 trust a brand  that's recommended by so many  dermatologists  so i think dermablend could probably  just put a bit more effort into  communicating this change in their  advice because  what's in my gms is very different from  what you would get  if you just look through the internet so  if i were producing a product like this  this is how i would test the claim i get  a bunch of consumers to mix the pigment  drops into the sunscreens themselves  to see how much they mix and how they  mix it like how thoroughly  then i would replicate the worst case  scenarios in the lab with a bunch of  different sunscreen formulations  and then test them on people and see  what the spf is see if the spf drops  if the sps stays around the same for all  the common sunscreen formulations then i  would be happy with that claim  if it doesn't because there are a lot of  different sunscreen formulas there are  lots of different  technologies used in different  sunscreens so yeah i'd like to see  that done on a range of sunscreens and  have it stay  good so i don't know if that's possible  i'm guessing the dross would have to  have some spf protection in them for  that to work  and yeah there's just so many different  formulations with sunscreens  that i think it would be really  difficult to make sure it didn't  destabilize  any of them i'm not sure if it's  possible but  maybe it is that's it for today remember  these are just my opinions on the claims  from these companies with the  information i have  maybe there's some information i don't  have that would be relevant as well  let me know if you agree or disagree in  the comments also let me know if you  have other spf products with weird  claims that you want me to go through  i hope you liked this video if you did  give it a thumbs up you can subscribe to  my channel  as well check me out on instagram and  check out my blog  and i will see you next time  you
 

